resources.string:
Hiding lowers the odds of being noticed; it doesn't make them zero. StegPony can't protect you from:

• someone who has the original photo you hid in;
• a detector trained on photos from your own camera, especially with a lot hidden;
• someone who knows StegPony is installed and insists on a second passphrase;
• a forensic examination of your unlocked phone;
• anyone who sees whom you send images to, and when. StegPony hides what you send, not that you sent it.
